AUDIT step 6: power.  Static currents [AFE/review/sim/f1_bias_op.log, rows 1k_3L]; digital energy per SCLK cycle = LibreLane power.rpt / 2 MHz (tt 79.6 pJ, ss 125 C 3.0 V 67.5 pJ, ff -40 C 3.6 V 96.2 pJ; default data activity,
clock and flop-clock-pin power dominate: 97 %); 160 SCLK per frame, 4000 frames/s.  DOUT pad: C_load ASSUMED, 36 rising edges per frame (144 data bits x 0.25), E = C V^2 per rising edge.

corner                 |     amps    bias   vhalf |  digital     cmp     DAC DOUT15pF  dyn_sum |   RECORD     IDLE | uA record (avg from the pad)
typical    27 C 3.3 V  |   1817.9    18.4   169.2 |     54.0    2.30    1.88     23.5     81.7 |   2087.2   2005.5 |   632.5
ff         85 C 3.3 V  |   2930.7    25.7   221.8 |     54.8    2.69    1.70     23.5     82.7 |   3260.9   3178.2 |   988.2
ss        -40 C 3.3 V  |   1137.0    13.4   131.5 |     55.4    2.23    2.06     23.5     83.2 |   1365.2   1282.0 |   413.7
ff        -40 C 3.6 V  |   2126.0    24.0   234.4 |     65.2    2.69    1.85     28.0     97.8 |   2482.3   2384.5 |   689.5
ss        125 C 3.0 V  |   1773.4    15.0   125.0 |     45.8    2.23    1.87     19.4     69.4 |   1982.8   1913.4 |   660.9
  all in uW.  RECORD = STIMULATE (frames still read) = RESET (RST_AMP held) : the analog current does not depend on the mode; IDLE = SCLK stopped (static only).
  SCLK 2 MHz and 3 MHz give the same average (160 clocks per frame at both).  If the host lets SCLK free-run: digital = 159 uW at 2 MHz, 239 uW at 3 MHz (tt) instead of ~54 uW.
  DOUT load 10 / 20 pF: 15.7 / 31.4 uW at 3.3 V.  One-shot timer legs: 8 x ~2 nA while the routing switch is open (negligible).

PEAK / TRANSIENT (ESTIMATE):
  digital charge per SCLK cycle = 24.1 pC (tt), 26.7 pC (ff -40 C 3.6 V), 22.5 pC (ss 125 C 3.0 V); X2 S4 assumed 1.5 pC per converting ADC per edge = 12 pC at most.
  comparator 1.8-2.6 pC per decision in ~2 ns (about 1 mA peak each, staggered); DAC 2.9 pC on the MSB trial; DOUT pad 15 pF x 3.3 V = 50 pC per edge in 5-10 ns: 5-10 mA peak, only during read-out (after the conversions).
  peak from the pad pair therefore ~10-25 mA for a few ns; on-chip decap 0.225 nF: 24 pC -> ~0.1 V if taken from 0.225 nF alone, 45 mV measured in X2 S4 with 12 pC [AFE/adc/sim/x2_s4_summary.log].

